{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>He is Aharon and Moshe.</b> He placed Aharon before Moshe because he was older than him in years, and afterward it says 'He is Moshe and Aharon' — he placed Moshe before him because he is greater than him in prophecy. So too we find that he placed Yehoshua before Kalev, because he was greater than him in prophecy, and he placed Kalev before Yehoshua because he was greater than him in lineage, as it is written (Numbers 14:38) ״ויהושע בן נון וכלב בן יפונה חיו מן האנשים״ and it is written (ibid.) ״כי אם כלב בן יפנה ויהושע בן נון״. And likewise Scripture placed the heavens before the earth for their preeminence, for the intelligible created beings are more honored than the corporeal ones, because these are eternal while those perish and pass away. And it also placed the earth before the heavens, because there is the Temple there and the Shekhinah dwells within it, and our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: 'the root of the Shekhinah was among the lower ones,' and this is what is written (Genesis 2:4) ״אלה תולדות השמים והארץ בהבראם ביום עשות ה' אלהים ארץ ושמים״. And the reason it repeated 'And it was on the day HaShem spoke to Moshe in the land of Egypt' is because it mentioned above <b>They brought the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt by their hosts,</b> and the command was upon both of them to bring them out of the land of Egypt; therefore it comes to teach you that the speech was with Moshe alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:36.330799166Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}